          "final_text_tail": "\n\nDone. The task is fully implemented in `llama-index-core/llama_index/core/base/llms/types.py`:\n\n1. **Added `encoding` field** (types.py:58): `encoding: Literal[\"base64\", \"raw\"] = \"base64\"` \u2014 defaults to `\"base64\"` to preserve existing behavior; pydantic rejects any other value.\n2. **Updated `image_to_base64` validator** (types.py:86-105): still guesses the mimetype, but only base64-encodes when `encoding == \"base64\"`; with `encoding=\"raw\"` the bytes are kept as-is.\n3. **Updated `resolve_image`** (types.py:113-120): branches on `encoding` so raw blocks resolve correctly in both raw and base64 modes.\n\nVerification:\n- All 12 existing tests in `tests/base/llms/test_types.py` pass.\n- Sanity checks confirmed: default blocks encode to base64 as before; `encoding=\"raw\"` keeps raw bytes; mimetype guessing works in both modes; `resolve_image`/`resolve_image(as_base64=True)` return correct bytes in both modes; invalid encoding values raise validation errors.\n\nNote: the `get_image_mimetype` refactor visible in `git diff` was a pre-existing uncommitted working-tree change, not part of my edit. (A flaky NLTK network download at import time made some test runs hang; I verified results using a temporary no-op `nltk.download` pytest plugin, since removed.)",
